{"format":1,"key":"zone:ironforge","path":"/lore/zone/ironforge","name":"Ironforge","kind":"zone","label":"Capital","zone":{"key":"ironforge","name":"Ironforge","path":"/lore/zone/ironforge"},"levels":"","description":"Carved into the heart of Ironforge Mountain in snowy Dun Morogh, Ironforge is the ancestral capital of the Bronzebeard dwarves and an unassailable…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:ironforge","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Carved into the heart of Ironforge Mountain in snowy Dun Morogh, Ironforge is the ancestral capital of the Bronzebeard dwarves and an unassailable bastion of the Alliance. Centered on the molten heat of the Great Forge, this sprawling underground city serves as a bustling hub of commerce, industry, and ancient dwarven lore. Under the steadfast rule of King Magni Bronzebeard, it now also shelters the displaced gnomes of nearby Gnomeregan.","Ironforge was founded twenty-five hundred years ago when the first generation of dwarves awakened in Uldaman and journeyed west into Dun Morogh's jagged peaks. Delving into the tallest mountain, they built a massive shrine to their titan progenitor Khaz'goroth alongside the colossal Great Forge. Ever since, the city has expanded in concentric rings around that fiery hearth. Unlike surface capitals, Ironforge is entirely enclosed beneath stone ceilings, warmed by roaring hearths and subterranean rivers of molten magma. Its fortified gates and cavernous depths have proven near-impregnable throughout centuries of war.","For generations, three dwarven clans coexisted within Ironforge: the Bronzebeards, the Wildhammers, and the Dark Irons. When High King Modimus Anvilmar died in 230 BDP, a bitter civil war erupted for dominion over the mountain. The Bronzebeard clan prevailed and expelled their rivals. Later, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan led a vengeful Dark Iron siege that penetrated to the heart of Ironforge before being repulsed by Bronzebeard forces. Thaurissan accidentally summoned Ragnaros the Firelord to the south, shattering the Redridge Mountains and dooming his own host. The Bronzebeards have held undisputed control of Ironforge ever since.","During the Second War, the Bleeding Hollow orc clan overran much of Khaz Modan, but Ironforge held firm behind its sealed gates until the Alliance of Lordaeron lifted the siege. Bound by this debt of honor, King Magni Bronzebeard pledged Ironforge's eternal loyalty to the Alliance, standing firm even when kingdoms like Gilneas and Quel'Thalas abandoned it. In the Third War, Magni mourned the loss of his brother Muradin in Northrend. Today, Ironforge remains one of the Alliance's fiercest bulwarks.","Following the tragic fall of Gnomeregan to trogg invaders and irradiation, King Magni opened Ironforge's gates to thousands of gnome refugees. Under High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, the exiles established Tinker Town, carving out a buzzing technological haven within the stone city. Coupled with the subterranean Deeprun Tram connecting Ironforge directly to Stormwind City, the dwarven stronghold has transformed into a lively crossroads of dwarven steelcraft and gnomish ingenuity."],"hash":"d8192b","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"eac1efdf7c","sec":158},"female-narrator":{"sha":"bc6f265c2c","sec":167}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Ironforge","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ironforge"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/magni-bronzebeard","n":"Magni Bronzebeard","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/great-forge","n":"Great Forge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/tinker-town","n":"Tinker Town","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/deeprun-tram","n":"Deeprun Tram","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/high-seat","n":"High Seat","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/dunmorogh","n":"Dun Morogh","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/gelbin-mekkatorque","n":"Gelbin Mekkatorque","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/topic/bronzebeard-clan","n":"Bronzebeard clan","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/quest/91758-follow-that-kobold","n":"Follow That